==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|de|Schade}} {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|scado}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*skaþô}}. Confer {{cog|nl|schade}}, {{cog|en|scathe}}, {{cog|sv|skada}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃaːdən/|[ˈʃaːdən]|[ˈʃaːdn̩]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-schaden.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Schadens|Schäden}}

# [[damage]]; [[harm]]
#: ''Das Auto hat einen '''Schaden.''''' - “The car is damaged.”
#: ''Er hat seiner Frau nie '''Schaden''' zugefügt.'' - “He has never done any harm to his wife.”
# {{lb|de|colloquial|informal}} [[mental]] [[problem]] {{qualifier|in the sense of “crazy”}}
#: ''Der hat doch ’n '''Schaden.''''' – “He must be out of his mind.''”

